# nektos/act configuration example
#
# Copy this file into the root of the repository you run with Act/Run:
#
#   cp .actrc.example .actrc
#   cd /path/to/your-repository
#   act --version
#   act workflow_dispatch -W .github/workflows/your-caller.yml
#
# Only the *calling* workflow belongs after -W. For example, if your caller
# references owner/repo/.github/workflows/build.yml@main, do not pass
# build.yml to -W unless that file actually exists in this repository.
#
# This example deliberately has no enabled flags: it is safe to copy on
# Docker Desktop, OrbStack, Linux, and Apple Silicon without presuming a
# particular network, architecture, image, or artifacts directory.
#
# Uncomment only options you need. act config options are not shell commands;
# keep each enabled option on its own line. Check 'act --help' for your version.

# ─── Runner image ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Act/Run can supply a default runner image. To override it yourself:
# -P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
#
# Pull newer images when appropriate (the default behavior depends on act).
# Avoid disabling pulls unless you manage the image locally and know it exists.
# --pull=false

# ─── Apple Silicon / ARM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# If act warns about an Apple M-series processor, and your workflow expects
# x86-64 images/tools, enable AMD64 emulation (may run more slowly).
# This option does NOT fix errors about missing .github/workflows/*.yml files.
# --container-architecture linux/amd64
#
# Use the native architecture when your runner image and dependencies support it.

# ─── Docker network (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only enable if this Docker network already exists:
#   docker network ls
# --network my-existing-network
#
# Without a custom network, act manages ordinary container networking.
# Inside a container, localhost refers to that container.

# ─── Execution options (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Limit concurrent jobs on smaller development machines:
# --concurrent-jobs 2
#
# Store artifacts locally. Create this directory first, choose a location
# appropriate for your machine, and keep it out of source control:
# --artifact-server-path /tmp/act-artifacts
#
# Container reuse may retain state between runs; enable only when wanted.
# --reuse

# ─── Credentials ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Do NOT put secrets or tokens in this file.
# Keep .secrets untracked and pass it when needed:
#   act workflow_dispatch -W .github/workflows/your-caller.yml --secret-file .secrets
#
# Troubleshooting:
#   ls .github/workflows/
#   act --version
#   docker info
#
# Documentation: docs/02-guides/act-configuration/page.mdx
